    },
    {
      "objective": "Objective 2: Reduce Customer Acquisition Cost by 20%",
      "verdict": "OFF-TRACK — KR 2.1 at 55% (pace 0.55) inherits compounded risk from KR 1.3 scope failure; KR 2.2 and 2.3 are on track",
      "narrative": "KR 2.2 (attribution model, 80%) and KR 2.3 (Google Ads CPC, 90%) are both on track and close to completion — these represent genuine Q2 execution wins for Webb's team. The problem is KR 2.1: a CAC of $42.80 against a $38.40 target at quarter close, pace ratio 0.55, is off-track. More importantly, the KR's own documentation states it depended on the DTC channel being live, because DTC has 40% lower CAC than paid social. DTC did not launch in its intended form. This is not solely a KR 2.1 execution failure — it is a dependency miss propagated from Objective 1. The $42.80 CAC represents the counterfactual where DTC was a waitlist, not a converting channel. A Q3 DTC checkout launch would partially recover this objective if the attribution model (KR 2.2) is complete and operational.",
      "owner_action": "Marcus Webb to quantify the estimated CAC improvement from a live DTC checkout launch and incorporate it into Q3 planning assumptions by 2026-07-10, using the KR 2.2 attribution model once it clears QA."
    },
    {
      "objective": "Objective 3: Build Product Innovation Pipeline",
      "verdict": "AT-RISK — KR 3.1 complete; KR 3.2 partial miss with measurement gap on replacement; KR 3.3 measurement gap",
      "narrative": "KR 3.1 (consumer research, 100%) is a clean Q2 completion and provides the foundation for the pipeline. The innovation objective's problems lie in KRs 3.2 and 3.3. KR 3.2: the second concept failed technical feasibility, and a replacement concept was only entered into stage-gate 1 at week 11. There is no path to stage-gate 2 completion in the two remaining weeks of Q2, and no trend data exists for the replacement. This KR closes at 50% with a structural timing problem, not a measurement gap — the sequence of events is documented. KR 3.3 has had no update in seven weeks (since May 15). At quarter close, with only one of two provisional patents filed, this is both a performance gap (pace 0.50 = off-track) and a measurement gap — the second filing's status is unknown. Given that patent filing deadlines are often tied to publication or competitive timelines, the silence is concerning.",
      "owner_action": "Dr. Yasmin Torres to (a) provide immediate status of the second provisional patent filing by 2026-07-03, and (b) present a revised stage-gate timeline for the replacement concept at the Q3 kickoff meeting by 2026-07-10, including a realistic gate-2 target date."
    }
  ],
  "informational_updates": "KR 2.2 (unified attribution model) is in final QA and expected to complete shortly after Q2 close — this is a strong foundation for Q3 performance measurement improvements. KR 2.3 (Google Ads CPC reduction) achieved 13.8% of the 15% target, closing 90% complete — a near-win that demonstrates the paid media team's optimization capability and provides a basis for similar efforts in Q3. KR 1.1's NorthMart deal in the final three weeks shows that large distribution deals can close quickly when negotiation momentum builds — a pattern worth replicating in Q3 to close the remaining 224 stores."
